course: dictionary
lesson: 9280
title: What is a spaniel?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A spaniel is a type of dog. You can spot one by its long, soft ears that hang down and its silky coat. Some well-known kinds are the cocker spaniel, the springer spaniel and the King Charles spaniel.
explain: Writers use words like spaniel to paint a picture. In «My dog (a spaniel) loves walks», the words in brackets tell you which dog it is. You can lift them out and the sentence still works: «My dog loves walks».
explain: Context helps you too. Spaniels are friendly family pets and good working dogs that sniff out birds. In stories they are loyal, eager companions, so a spaniel in a story is often a faithful friend.
fact: A spaniel is a noun: one spaniel, two spaniels.
fact: «Spaniel» means a dog with long soft ears that hang down and a silky coat.
fact: Breeds of spaniel include the cocker spaniel, the springer spaniel and the King Charles spaniel.
fact: Spaniels are popular, friendly family pets, and good at sniffing out birds.
fact: Springer spaniels also help police sniff out things.
exercise: «My dog (a spaniel) loves walks.» What is a spaniel? | A bird that sniffs for food | A type of cat with a long tail | *A dog with long soft ears that hang down | A bowl for water
exercise: Which of these is a breed of spaniel? | Labrador | *King Charles | Beagle | Poodle
exercise: «The eager spaniel ran to the door.» Find and copy the word that tells you the spaniel is keen and ready. | door | the | ran | *eager
test: Which of these is a spaniel breed? | *Springer | Dachshund | Poodle | Husky
test: Which feature helps you recognise a spaniel? | Short, spiky fur | *Long soft ears that hang down | Wings on its back | A curly tail like a pig
exam: Which sentence correctly says what a spaniel is? | A spaniel is a kind of sofa | *A spaniel is a dog with long soft ears that hang down | A spaniel is a bowl for the dog's food | A spaniel is a bird that flies at night
